  "_comment": "Which reading a small word with more than one takes, decided once from what stands round it (services/syntax/particles.py walks it; the card, the picture and the case rules all read the answer). A branch splits on one particle axis: `word` the word itself, `next` what follows it (an indefinite noun: no ال, no name, no pronoun on it), `negated` a negation before it, `joins` the noun after it in the case of a noun before it, `opens` the noun after it with a khabar of its own after it. `tool_next` the word after it is خلا، عدا or حاشا; `raf` the noun after it typed in raf' (the noun of لا of the genus never is), `told` what stands after that noun: a noun, its khabar (لا رجلٌ أفضلُ منك: لا المشبهة بليس), or anything else (لا خوفٌ عليهم: the noun is a مبتدأ). `wonder` ما before a verb of the wonder shape (closed_words.json wonder). `asks` ما or من asks (Tasheel 2.4.7 p47): a noun, pronoun or pointer follows as its مبتدأ and no verb, ظرف, preposition or إلا comes after it (ما اسمك، من أنت), or a verb of informing with its pronoun is followed by a second question word (وما أدراك ما يوم الدين); ما عندكم ينفد and من في البيت are not it. `restricted` an إلا comes after it in the clause (ما أنت إلا بشر). A leaf's `role` is the closed_words.json family it works as; `named` its name where the family card's own does not fit, `kind` when it is no حرف (إذا before a verb is a ظرف), `retag` the word class the parser's tag is written over with before the other words are read (ما قبل إلا is a particle, so إلا after it restricts). `starts` only a و or ف stands before it (إذن opens the answer); `shows` the mood the present verb after it shows (nasb, raf', other) or none where no present verb follows it directly (closed_words.json nasb_mudari `idhan_*`). إِذًا with a tanween is the lemma إذن (nasb_mudari `tanween_spells`), never the time word. A word with no branch here is read by its lists as before.",
